SSH VPN for OPNsense.

Adds tun/tap tunnels (PermitTunnel) to the built-in OPNsense SSH service
so Linux clients using NetworkManager-ssh
(https://github.com/danfruehauf/NetworkManager-ssh) can connect.
A drop-in in /usr/local/etc/ssh/sshd_config.d enables this for root only;
no second sshd instance is started.

Each client is bound to its public key, a fixed tun/tap unit and a
pair of tunnel addresses. The Linux "ip" commands sent by
NetworkManager-ssh are ignored; the firewall configures its side of
the tunnel itself using FreeBSD ifconfig.
